From: Ryan Chen <rchen14b@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 16 Mar 2026 12:00:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] net: export br_fdb_find_rcu

Export br_fdb_find_rcu() so netfilter flow offload can check if a
destination MAC is known in the bridge FDB.

This is a prerequisite for nft_flow_offload bridging support.

Note: the __dev_fill_forward_path() export this patch used to carry is
no longer needed -- upstream backport 706-01 ("net: pass
net_device_path_ctx to dev_fill_forward_path") already passes an
external ctx into dev_fill_forward_path().

Signed-off-by: Ryan Chen <rchen14b@gmail.com>
---
 net/bridge/br_fdb.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

--- a/net/bridge/br_fdb.c
+++ b/net/bridge/br_fdb.c
@@ -262,6 +262,7 @@ struct net_bridge_fdb_entry *br_fdb_find
 {
 	return fdb_find_rcu(&br->fdb_hash_tbl, addr, vid);
 }
+EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(br_fdb_find_rcu);
 
 /* When a static FDB entry is added, the mac address from the entry is
  * added to the bridge private HW address list and all required ports
